. The factorial of a number n, denoted by n!, is the product of all positive integers less than or equal to n.

```javascript
function factorial(n) {
    let result = 1;
    for (let i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
        result *= i;
    }
    return result;
}

console.log(factorial(5));  // Output: 120
console.log(factorial(10));  // Output: 3628800
```

